{
 "section_summary": "This section records debate over labor rights and union organization in occupied Japan, including Roger Baldwin’s proposals, State Department correspondence, Soviet criticism, and U.S. rebuttals. It also contains ILO Convention No. 87, a detailed SCAP assessment of Japanese labor conditions in 1949, and a conversation with two Japanese parliamentarians about labor and land reform. The SCAP reports emphasize unemployment, falling real wages, union politics, and the risks of government, employer, or Communist control of unions.",
